From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:13:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] shermes: group outlined helpers into bounded C
 translation units

Keep the no-inline functions introduced for large generated control-flow graphs, but stop requiring one native frontend invocation per helper. Group up to 64 helpers from one owning function while accounting for the shard byte target, shared state layout, extern prologue, and referenced-function declarations.

The wrapper remains an independent translation unit with its explicit optimization policy, exception handling, and rooted register state. Fragment metadata continues to enumerate translation units in wrapper call-site order. Object cache identities still include every generated byte.

Extend the bundle regression test to verify grouped definitions, complete wrapper-call coverage, and optimized execution while retaining structural O0 wrappers. Both focused bundle tests pass. An isolated large-bundle compile also passes the consumer manifest validator and Wasmtime AOT compilation without exceeding the function-local limit.
